{{!
    Overrides the ruby generator's built-in README.mustache. Passed as
    -t templates/ruby; templates absent from that directory fall back to the
    ones embedded in the jar, which is why only this file exists.

    NOTE: a mustache comment ends at its first closing brace pair, so no
    variable or partial tag may appear in this block. Naming one here silently
    ends the comment and renders the remainder as markup.

    Four defects in the built-in template motivated the override. It tells the
    reader to build the gem by hand or install it from a git URL rather than
    from the registry the gem is published to; it names an internal generator
    class; it fills the authorization example with credential placeholders that
    read as real instructions; and it carries a build date that would churn
    this file on every run.

    Unlike the python generator there is no common_README partial to defer to,
    so the endpoint, model and authorization sections at the bottom are copied
    from the built-in template. A generator upgrade can change them there
    without changing them here.

    The Getting Started example is hand-written rather than looped over the
    first operation, which is what produced the credential placeholders. It
    calls the auth endpoint, so a spec change that renames that operation will
    make it wrong without failing anything -- check it on a generator or spec
    upgrade. It sets no host on purpose: the gate below rejects any host but
    production, and the client already defaults to it.

    scripts/verify_readme.py gates the rendered output in CI, on both the PR
    and the publish path.
